  "final_verdict": {
    "answer": "NO long-only, cost-adjusted version of the 1-day PEAD continuation has positive expectancy. The +28.8bp is a SHORT-side effect (shorting mega-cap missers), NOT an illiquidity effect.",
    "long_leg_is_beta_not_alpha": "Top-quintile beater days are UP-market days (universe EW index +15.8bp, broad EW index +12.6bp on those days vs +2.6bp on misser days). The raw +20-21bp long return is almost entirely this drift; the market-adjusted alpha is +4.1bp (universe-adj) / +8.7bp (broad-adj), both with day-clustered t < 1 (0.35 / 0.91) -- statistically indistinguishable from zero.",
    "long_leg_dies_at_cost": "Broad-adjusted top-quintile +8.7bp -> net -1.3bp at 10bp RT, -11.3bp at 20bp. Universe-adjusted +4.1bp -> -0.9bp at 5bp. No positive net expectancy at any realistic 5-20bp cost.",
    "short_leg_is_the_effect": "Bottom-quintile missers: -25.1bp market-adjusted, day-clustered t = -3.73 (highly significant). ~87% of the +28.8bp spread is the short leg (top +4.1bp vs bottom -25.1bp). Harvesting it requires SHORTING (borrow/locate), unavailable to a long-only account.",
    "not_illiquid": "Universe is 149 mega/large-caps. >$10 price filter keeps 89% of top-quintile events; >$50M dollar-volume keeps 94%. The long alpha stays ~+1-5bp (t<0.5) under every liquidity filter. The short leg is in liquid, easy-to-borrow mega-caps -- it is short-side, not illiquid.",
    "concentration_long_leg_fragile": "Long leg is NOT broad: top 10 symbols (2.2% of events) account for 50% of the positive contribution; removing them flips the long leg market-adjusted mean to -8.7bp. Removing the top 10 dates flips it to -3.9bp. The weak +4bp is a handful of names/dates.",
    "parameter_stability": "Top-bucket market-adjusted alpha across 2/3/4/5/6/10 buckets: +4.0/+4.4/+6.3/+4.5/+3.7/+15.8bp with t = 0.69/1.23/0.79/0.40/-0.05/1.46 -- none significant. The SPREAD stays significant (t 3.2-4.1) in every bucket count purely because the bottom bucket is significant; the long bucket never is.",
    "best_long_candidate_still_fails": "Post-market top-quintile (close entry) is the strongest long leg: +16.1bp universe-adj (t=1.05) / +20.5bp broad-adj (t=1.39), bootstrap CI spans zero -- not significant, and <20bp means negative net at 20bp cost.",
    "caveat_nextopen_2day": "A post-market next-OPEN entry held 2 days (open D+1 -> close D+2) shows raw +55.6bp (t=2.38) / broad-adj +47.8bp (t=2.16), positive net at 20bp. FLAGGED NOT VALIDATED: (1) the broad index is close-to-close so it cannot correctly adjust an open-entry position (adjustment under-corrects by ~1 day of market); (2) it is a 2-day hold, not the 1-day trade; (3) single best config among many = multiple-testing risk. Needs a clean intraday market proxy before being trusted.",
    "bottom_line": "Strictly short-side. Any long-only buy-beaters version is beta + noise and negative after cost."
  }
